{
  "sn12.1:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.1 ",
  "sn12.1:0.2": "1. The Buddhas ",
  "sn12.1:0.3": "Dependent Origination ",
  "sn12.1:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn12.1:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn12.1:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "sn12.1:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "sn12.1:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn12.1:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn12.1:1.7": "“Mendicants, I will teach you dependent origination. ",
  "sn12.1:1.8": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "sn12.1:1.9": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn12.1:1.10": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn12.1:2.1": "“And what is dependent origination? ",
  "sn12.1:2.2": "Ignorance is a requirement for choices. ",
  "sn12.1:2.3": "Choices are a requirement for consciousness. ",
  "sn12.1:2.4": "Consciousness is a requirement for name and form. ",
  "sn12.1:2.5": "Name and form are requirements for the six sense fields. ",
  "sn12.1:2.6": "The six sense fields are requirements for contact. ",
  "sn12.1:2.7": "Contact is a requirement for feeling. ",
  "sn12.1:2.8": "Feeling is a requirement for craving. ",
  "sn12.1:2.9": "Craving is a requirement for grasping. ",
  "sn12.1:2.10": "Grasping is a requirement for continued existence. ",
  "sn12.1:2.11": "Continued existence is a requirement for rebirth. ",
  "sn12.1:2.12": "Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death, sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadne